      "id": "clm_01M4VS7B2R1TBGMPWVSNTQZ9XD",
      "statement": "Nehemiah's king was Artaxerxes I, so his commission fell in 445 BC.",
      "layer": "reconstruction",
      "passage": "Neh.2.1",
      "classification": "strongly_supported",
      "reasoning": "The Elephantine letter of 408/407 shows Bigvai as governor of Judah and the sons of Sanballat active, so Nehemiah's 32nd year (Neh 13:6) must belong to Artaxerxes I (433), placing the twentieth year in 445 (Cowley); Keil and the commentators read the same. Josephus's Xerxes is out of line with both the biblical names and the papyri.",
